Description
Tenant configuration rendering engine for Juniper EVPN-VXLAN AI fabrics.

It reads the tenants_dynamic.yaml file created by create_dynamic_yaml-with-gpu-server.py and generates:
- A single combined configuration (all-tenants-dynamic.conf) with all tenants, and
- Per-tenant, per-leaf configuration files (e.g., TenantA-STRIPE1_LEAF1.conf, TenantA-STRIPE2_LEAF1.conf) that include only the interfaces present on each leaf.
  The script uses a Jinja2 template (tenant-template-no-comments.j2) to generate Junos set-style configuration lines per tenant, per interface, and per leaf.
This approach allows for deterministic, automated configuration generation with proper variable substitution for RDs, VRFs, IPv6 addresses, etc.
Functionality Overview
When executed, the script follows these steps:
Step 1: Cleans Previously Generated Files
Deletes any pre-existing generated files that match:
-STRIPE.conf (per-tenant/leaf configs)
tenants-STRIPE*.conf (older aggregate files, optional)
This ensures a clean slate before generating new config files.
Step 2: Load Tenant YAML
Reads tenants_dynamic.yaml, a yaml containing all the parameters generated per tenant by the create_dynamic_yaml-with-gpu-server.py script
Step 3: Loads Jinja2 Template
Reads tenant-template-no-comments.j2, a text-based Jinja2 template used to render tenant configs.
Variables like {{ TENANT_NAME }}, {{ VNI }}, {{ RD_ROUTER_ID }}, etc. are populated with data from the YAML.
Step 4: Generates Config Files
Configuration for each tenant is rendered using the Jinja2 template and the contents of tenants_dynamic.yaml

The resulting config block is written to tenants-{leaf}.conf and appended to the all-tenants-dynamic.conf file.

